---
import Layout from '../layouts/doc.astro';
import { ThemeAppMock } from '../components/theme-app-mock';
---

<Layout title="Themes">

<h1>Themes</h1>

<p>Same components, different world. <strong>Pick one in the sidebar.</strong></p>

<div class="theme-showcase">
  <ThemeAppMock client:load />
</div>

<h2>Dark Mode</h2>

<p>Every theme ships with a dark variant. Import one CSS file and dark mode works automatically — no flags, no extra imports, no toggle configuration required.</p>

<h3>How it works</h3>

<p>Each theme file contains both light and dark tokens. Dark mode activates via <code>@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)</code>, following the user's OS setting.</p>

<pre><code>{`/* Just import a theme — dark mode is built in */
@import "@beaket/ui/themes/porcelain.css";`}</code></pre>

<p>Shadows auto-flip through token references. No overrides needed.</p>

<h3>Manual control</h3>

<p>To override OS detection, set <code>beaket-color-scheme</code> in <code>localStorage</code>:</p>

<pre><code>{`// Force dark
localStorage.setItem("beaket-color-scheme", "dark");

// Force light
localStorage.setItem("beaket-color-scheme", "light");

// Follow OS (default)
localStorage.removeItem("beaket-color-scheme");`}</code></pre>

<h3>Theme personalities</h3>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Theme</th><th>Light</th><th>Dark</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Porcelain</td><td>Industrial precision</td><td>X-ray lightbox</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>Golden hour library</td><td>Whiskey bar at midnight</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Marigold</td><td>Screen-printed poster</td><td>Neon signs at night</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Eucalyptus</td><td>Enterprise titanium</td><td>Mission control</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

</Layout>

<style>
  :global(.main) {
    max-width: none;
  }
  .theme-showcase {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
</style>
